      "writtenOn": "2022-08-24T13:10:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There seems to be a large amount of code that could be shared with the existing single-frame encode function. Is there any way to rearrange this to avoid the copy-paste?\n\nAlso: Do we need to worry about color spaces? (I see that the single-frame encode checks for a color space and embeds an ICC profile. We\u0027d need to ensure that all the frames have the same color space, but we ought to do that, right?)\n\n+scroggo, who may have other input.",
      "revId": "e3ce613f91acf7e58a3114d04c7376ea99d7e1b9",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fea5971a_a7493708",
